    "title": "Strong second half helps Warsaw girls pull away at Bellmont - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Josh Ayen ,\n56 minutes ago\nDECATUR, Ind. (WANE) – In a battle between two state title contenders, 4A No. 4 Warsaw overcame a halftime deficit to top 3A No. 4 Bellmont, 72-57, on Wednesday at the Teepee.\nButler commit Joslyn Bricker led the Tigers with 32 points, while Miami (Ohio) commit Brooke Zartman scored 20. Alexis Neely added 13 points to round out Warsaw’s double-digit scorers. Mary Bleke led Bellmont with 22 points, while Ashley Bleke poured in 16.\nTrailing 31-29 at halftime, Warsaw blitzed Bellmont in the third quarter by outscoring the Braves, 21-8. The Tigers opened the third quarter on an 11-3 run, which included a pair of buckets from Bricker and a 3-pointer from Zartman. Bellmont stayed within 10 points early in the fourth quarter, but Warsaw pulled away down the stretch to come away with the road victory.\nWarsaw wraps up the regular season with a 23-2 record. The Tigers await the winner of a first-round sectional game between Elkhart and Goshen on Feb. 6 to tip off postseason play. Bellmont (17-3) wraps up the regular season on Saturday at Leo before tipping off sectional play with a semifinal game between New Haven or Marion a week from Friday.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
